      <groundspeak:long_description html="True"> </groundspeak:long_description>
      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>IN CAIRN MARKED BY 5&#39; TALL SP 

BCP742- Cardinal Divide. Above ground level in a rock cairn, marked by a 5&#39; tall yellow survey post.
Park at N52 53.676 W117 14.864 
</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="673800899">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-03-31T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="5323897">brendan714</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP742 Cardinal Divide

N 52° 53.196 W 117° 17.500&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Logging a few 'found its' on brass caps I've found previously before I won't be able to do so (&lt;a href="http://forums.groundspeak.com/GC/index.php?showtopic=343632&amp;pid=5645061&amp;st=0&amp;#entry5645061" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;see attached announcement&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the coolest places I've ever been!  I visited the Cardinal Divide with my fiancee GeoJamie22 - partly for fun, and partly to visit a physical cache I had recently adopted.  I noticed the survey marker (an unpublished marker, not an ASCM) at the top of a prominent hill we hiked up.  Wow, what a great spot!  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Again, incredible views from the cap site!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I suggested to OFTH that this location would make a great addition to the brass cap page - and I think it certainly is a great addition! Thanks for adding this one OFTH!

I first found the cap on August 24, 2016. I was hoping to get back to the location at some point to 'officially' log the cap, but by the time I do that I will not be able to log my found it online - so I will log it today. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="640317588">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-09-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP742 - Cardinal Divide&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Posted:&lt;/strong&gt; N52° 53.196' W117° 17.500'

&lt;strong&gt;My GPSr:&lt;/strong&gt; N52° 53.199' W117° 17.498'&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This cap was the first spark that started the obsession to make a return visit to this awesome place. dronnord, VP and I made the trek out today had just a great time finding a Sleepy_hollow cache &quot;along the way&quot; and then this cap and the Cardinal Divide Beauty cache close by. The story of the trek is in the &lt;a href="https://www.geocaching.com/seek/log.aspx?LUID=7777dd53-3e86-4f08-af01-41cba41cc0dd" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Cardinal Divide Beauty cache find log&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thanks very much for the cap and luring us out for memorable adventure!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="640160818">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-09-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1298988">dronnord</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP742 - Cardinal Divide&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;N52 53.197  W117 17.499 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;elev = 2173.6&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTBCP in a truly spectacular setting. 10 km round trip in 3 hours on the ground. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was my 300th Cap find and my 4700 cache found.The 300th BCP was planned but I never planned on the double it just worked out that way. Funny how that works.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="640070188">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-09-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="403873">Viajero Perdido</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP742 - Cardinal Divide&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&quot;Do we have to move all those rocks?&quot;

&quot;Yep&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bingo.  Where else could it be?  Thanks for the mountain cap, always my favourite kind.  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="639186845">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="50.886600" lon="-117.291667" />
          <groundspeak:date>2016-09-23T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="321730">Sleepy_hollow</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP742 - Cardinal Divide&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a middle of the night start (okay early morning start if you're Strider's Ride) from Calgary, a short stop to pick up SR, we made it to the Cardinal Divide parking area by 11:00 am. We had made a number of stops on the way up the Forestry Trunk to pick up caches placed by hiking granny and check out the terrific fall colours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Once in the parking area the route to the cap site was pretty straight forward and soon we were taking pictures from the view point and rebuilding the rock cairn containing the cap. Great little spot - so unique and off the beaten track - thanks OFTH for setting it up!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
    </groundspeak:cache>
  </wpt>
</gpx>
